# Box art drive for the landing-page games carousel (site/demos/box-art.mjs).
#
# Mouse.Move coordinates are logical window points (the capture pins the window
# to 640x400) and the camera turns on their DELTAS, so the run below settles the
# aim DOWN onto the target line over half a second and then leaves the pointer
# alone: the only camera motion left is the recoil spring's climb under sustained
# fire. That is deliberate — a panning camera changes every pixel of every frame,
# which no palette-quantized GIF can compress into a card-sized file.
#
# The weapon is full-auto, so one `Mouse.Left down` is a sustained burst: the
# targets go down, the muzzle flashes, the gun climbs. R reloads once the
# magazine is out, so a longer capture window still has something happening.
# The window the box-art recipe captures is named in site/demos/box-art.mjs.
#
#   functor -d examples/shooting-range run native --input-script boxart.script \
#     --script-dt 0.0166667 --capture-at-frame 100 --capture-frame /tmp/sr.png

0 Mouse.Move 320 200
4 Mouse.Move 320 203
8 Mouse.Move 320 206
12 Mouse.Move 320 209
16 Mouse.Move 320 212
20 Mouse.Move 320 215
24 Mouse.Move 320 218
24 Mouse.Left down
190 Mouse.Left up
196 R down
197 R up
230 Mouse.Left down
360 Mouse.Left up
